In JavaScript:
```javascript
function add(a, b) {
  return a + b;
}
// or: const add = (a, b) => a + b;
```
A function has a name, parameters and a body that returns a result.

In Java:
```java
String full = first + " " + last;
String full2 = first.concat(" ").concat(last);
```
The + operator joins strings; concat is the method form, and StringBuilder is better inside loops.
